WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.041
Do you play, Mrs Bird?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.000
What's behind this organ?

00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:16.583
Oh, nothing to be concerned about.

00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:21.208
What about the lights and the humming?

00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:23.625
It's just a secret room.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.750
A secret room?

00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:30.500
- Well, what have you got in there?
- Oh, well, I'm afraid I can't tell you.

00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:32.958
That's strange.

00:00:33.083 --> 00:00:36.250
I don't know what you're finding
strange about it, Mrs Bird.

00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:40.750
It's just a secret room behind an organ,
and I can't tell you what's inside it.

00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:42.541
Nothing suspicious about it.

00:00:44.208 --> 00:00:49.083
D'you know, that is the second time
you've used the word "suspicious"?

00:00:49.208 --> 00:00:50.666
Oh, is it?

00:00:50.791 --> 00:00:53.291
Well, the Lord moves
in suspicious ways.

00:00:53.416 --> 00:00:55.666
You mean "mysterious ways"?

00:00:56.333 --> 00:01:00.000
Oh! You know your scripture,
Mrs Bird. (Chuckles)

00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:01.625
Anyway, come along.
Time for Bingo!

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:05.041
Aye!

00:01:06.125 --> 00:01:07.625
Bingo!

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:10.416
(Mr Brown) Do you think
it will be much further, Paddington?

00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:14.125
(Paddington) Fairly sure
Rumi Rock should be just through here.

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.125
- Little bit further...
- Ooh! Oh!

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.208
Just along here...

00:01:19.875 --> 00:01:21.250
...I think.

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:25.833
This way.

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:29.583
Just... over here.

00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:32.291
Or here.

00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:34.875
- And... left. Oh, no!
- (Mrs Brown) Oh!

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.875
(Paddington) That is a cliff. Right.

00:01:37.666 --> 00:01:39.083
Yes, that is right.

00:01:42.833 --> 00:01:44.958
(Mr Brown) Paddington,
don't take this the wrong way,

00:01:45.083 --> 00:01:47.333
but are you sure
you know where we are?

00:01:47.458 --> 00:01:50.625
Oh, yes, Mr Brown. We are...

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.541
Well, perhaps a little...

00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:56.041
...lost.

00:01:56.166 --> 00:01:58.208
(Sighs) Marvellous!

00:01:58.333 --> 00:02:00.208
At least we've dried off.

00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:03.083
(Thunderclap)

00:02:09.666 --> 00:02:14.000
(Mrs Brown) I spy with my little eye

00:02:14.125 --> 00:02:16.458
something beginning with...

00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:18.416
- (Animal screeching)
- Whoa!

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.000
Doesn't matter.

00:02:23.125 --> 00:02:26.000
Let's do our best
to get some sleep,

00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:30.708
even if we are all completely drenched
in a snake-infested jungle.

00:02:30.833 --> 00:02:32.583
(Mrs Brown) What happened to
"embracing the risk"?

00:02:32.708 --> 00:02:35.833
(Mr Brown) I've tried that, Mary.
God knows I've tried.

00:02:35.958 --> 00:02:38.166
But we don't belong here.

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.458
And quite frankly,
neither does Paddington.

00:02:42.833 --> 00:02:44.375
(Thunder rumbling)

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.416
(Rain pattering)

00:02:58.875 --> 00:03:01.375
Where are you, Aunt Lucy?

00:03:07.208 --> 00:03:09.166
Aunt Lucy...

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.250
Aunt Lucy!

00:03:19.291 --> 00:03:20.791
(Gasps)

00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:26.875
Aunt Lucy!

00:03:31.125 --> 00:03:32.125
Aunt Lucy?

00:03:36.625 --> 00:03:39.000
I thought I'd... lost you.

00:03:39.666 --> 00:03:42.083
Oh, Paddington!

00:03:42.208 --> 00:03:47.125
Can't you see that it is you
who are lost?

00:03:48.041 --> 00:03:50.041
(Paddington) Aunt Lucy!

00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:52.125
- (Thunder rumbling)
- (Gasps)

00:03:58.666 --> 00:04:00.208
Mmm...

00:04:09.416 --> 00:04:12.208
Argh! Oh! (Grunting)

00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:14.291
- (Bird squawking)
- Sorry!

00:04:14.416 --> 00:04:17.208
Argh! (Screaming)

00:04:23.625 --> 00:04:25.958
Oh! You again!

00:04:33.041 --> 00:04:34.500
Oh!

00:04:54.791 --> 00:04:56.666
(Thunderclap)

00:05:00.583 --> 00:05:02.375
(Roaring)

00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:05.458
- (Twig snapping)
- (Gasps)

00:05:05.583 --> 00:05:08.291
Ha, little bear!

00:05:08.416 --> 00:05:09.875
(Paddington) Mr Hunter!

00:05:10.541 --> 00:05:11.958
Thank goodness you're safe!

00:05:12.708 --> 00:05:15.291
- Whatever happened to you and Gina?
- Welcome...

00:05:16.875 --> 00:05:18.041
...to Rumi Rock.

00:05:18.166 --> 00:05:21.958
(Gasps) This is Rumi Rock!
Is Aunt Lucy here?

00:05:22.583 --> 00:05:23.958
- No.
- Oh!

00:05:24.083 --> 00:05:26.041
But I think she was here.

00:05:26.791 --> 00:05:32.000
Remember I told you Rumi Rock
was the gateway to El Dorado?

00:05:32.541 --> 00:05:33.583
Yes...?

00:05:33.708 --> 00:05:37.125
That's why we can't find her here,
Paddington.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:42.125
Because she has already found
her way there.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.833
And what makes you think that,
Mr Hunter?

00:05:45.541 --> 00:05:47.000
(Chuckling)

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:54.625
(Gasps) You translated the Quipu!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:55.916
What does it say?

00:05:56.041 --> 00:05:59.458
It says, "At Rumi Rock...

00:06:00.666 --> 00:06:04.458
"...the bear will show the way."

00:06:07.083 --> 00:06:09.541
Right!
And what bear would that be?

00:06:12.166 --> 00:06:15.416
You-you-you tell me.
You are the bear.

00:06:16.125 --> 00:06:17.333
Mmm!

00:06:17.458 --> 00:06:19.166
I see!

00:06:19.291 --> 00:06:21.750
And there isn't another message
written on the back? Because sometimes...

00:06:21.875 --> 00:06:25.250
No, no, no, no, no!
It says, "The bear will show the way."

00:06:25.375 --> 00:06:27.708
Now, you... are the bear!

00:06:27.833 --> 00:06:29.750
That's a bear!

00:06:29.875 --> 00:06:33.250
This talisman's got a bear on it.
You know? So...

00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:37.916
This whole thing is really... beary!

00:06:38.041 --> 00:06:39.875
Yes, really quite beary.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.416
So, what do we do... Bear?

00:06:46.291 --> 00:06:51.708
I don't know, Mr Hunter,
but Aunt Lucy always says,

00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:58.083
"When you're faced with a problem,
sit down and put on your thinking cap."

00:06:59.083 --> 00:07:00.958
(Snapping)

00:07:01.083 --> 00:07:04.041
(Roaring)

00:07:04.166 --> 00:07:08.125
(Echoing)

